<h2><a name="PREPARE2">Data Format for Collections and Anthologies</a></h2>
Since people still ask this question, let's get it out of the
way first thing. The difference between a collection and an anthology
is this: a collection is a collection of short fiction by a single author;
an anthology is a collection of short fiction, each story written by a different
author. As always, there are exceptions, but for the most part the above
rule applies just fine.
<p>
Both collections and anthologies tend to group data into 3 files: either
COLLECTIONS, SHORTFICTION, and BOOKS; or ANTHOLOGIES, SHORTFICTION, and
BOOKS. As with novels above, introductory material may be placed in the
ESSAYS file. Some anthologies may consist purely of essays, in which 
case there would be no associated entries in the SHORTFICTION file at all,
with everything being placed in the ESSAYS file.
<p>
Here's an example of a collection by Rebecca Ore. Note that many of
the short fiction entries have multiple publication keys, indicating
publication elsewhere.

<pre>
    -- COLLECTIONS ------------
    Alien Bootlegger and Other Stories {
        AE=|Rebecca Ore|
        YR=|1993|
        PB=|ALBL1993|
    }

    -- ESSAYS -----------------
    Aliens and the Artificial Other {
        AE=|Rebecca Ore|
        YR=|1993|
        PB=|ALBL1993|
    }

    -- SHORTFICTION -----------
    Alien Bootlegger {
        AE=|Rebecca Ore|
        YR=|1993|
        PB=|ALBL1993,TYBSF11A,TYBSF11B|
    }
    The Tyrant That I Serve {
        AE=|Rebecca Ore|
        YR=|1993|
        PB=|ALBL1993|
    }
    Giant Flesh Holograms Keep My Baby's Eyes Warm {
        AE=|Rebecca Ore|
        YR=|1993|
        PB=|ALBL1993|
    }
    Farming in Virginia {
        AE=|Rebecca Ore|
        YR=|1993|
        PB=|ALBL1993|
    }
    Projectile Weapons {
        AE=|Rebecca Ore|
        YR=|1993|
        PB=|ALBL1993|
    }
    Ice-Gouged Lakes, Glacier-Bound Times {
        AE=|Rebecca Ore|
        YR=|1988|
        SL=|ss|
        PB=|AMAZJUL1988,ALBL1993|
    }

    -- BOOKS ------------------
    Alien Bootlegger and Other Stories{
        AB=|ALBL1993|
        AE=|Rebecca Ore|
        YR=|1993|
        PB=|Tor|
        IS=|0-312-85549-4|
        PP=|313|
        PR=|19.95|
        TP=|hc|
        CV=|Wayne Barlowe|
        NT=|[V]|
    }

</pre>
<h2><a name="PREPARE3">Data Format for Magazines</a></h2>
Magazine data can be far more complex than the other forms of
publication. There isn't anything inherently difficult about it,
but it can cross a large number of files.
<p>
In the most simplified form, a magazine usually crosses just 2
files: SHORTFICTION and ZINES. The ZINE file contains the publication
data, while the SHORTFICTION file is filled in just as with collections
or anthologies. For instance, the entries for the January 97 issue
of <i>Science Fiction Age</i> are:

<pre>
    -- ZINES ------------------
    Science Fiction Age, January 1997 {
        AB=|SFAGEJAN97|
        AE=|Scott Edelman|
        YR=|1997|
        PP=|106|
        PR=|$3.95|
        CV=|David Mattingly|
        NT=|Vol 5, No 2|
    }

    -- SHORTFICTION -----------
    Blind Eye {
        AE=|Jack Dann|
        YR=|1997|
        SL=|sf|
        PB=|SFAGEJAN97|
    }
    Sam and the Prudent Jurist {
        AE=|Ben Bova|
        YR=|1997|
        SL=|sf|
        PB=|SFAGEJAN97|
    }
    The Five Biographies of General Gerrhan {
        AE=|Don Webb|
        YR=|1997|
        SL=|sf|
        PB=|SFAGEJAN97|
    }

</pre>
There are a couple of notes here: First, it is customary to add the
the volume and issue number to the notes section of the ZINE entry.
Second, in order to duplicate a modern-era Table of Contents, the
story length is entered in the SL field. Preferred SL entries are
ss=short story, nt=novelette, nv=novella. If the magazine does not
publish the story lengths (as with SF Age), use a length of sf
(for short fiction). Failure to use the SL field will cause the 
content listing of the magazine to appear like a collection or
anthology.
<p>
<h3><a name="PREPARE3A">Essays</a></h3>
In addition to short fiction, there are usually articles and essays.
In general, we like to list titled articles and drop the rest. We
really don't need to fill in Isaac Asimov's bibliography with several
hundred essays titled "Editorial". These entries, as with collections
and anthologies, go into the ESSAYS file:

<pre>

    -- ESSAYS -----------------
    Living Space {
        AE=|Alan Dean Foster|
        YR=|1997|
        PB=|SFAGEJAN97|
        NT=|An artist's gallery of Barclay Shaw's illustrations.|
    }
</pre>

<h3><a name="PREPARE3B">Interior Artists</a></h3>
Interior artists can be tracked by placing entries in the
INTERIORS file. These should have some descriptive title
(usually the same as the story being illustrated):

<pre>

    -- INTERIORS --------------
    Blooming Ice {
        AE=|David Beck|
        YR=|1997|
        PB=|SFAGEJAN97|
    }
    Living Space {
        AE=|Barclay Shaw|
        YR=|1997|
        PB=|SFAGEJAN97|
        NT=|An artist's gallery of illustrations.|
    }
    The Jackdaw's Last Case {
        AE=|Tom Simonton|
        YR=|1997|
        PB=|SFAGEJAN97|
    }
</pre>

<h3><a name="PREPARE3C">Book Reviews</a></h3>
Books reviews can also be entered into the REVIEWS file. The AE
field should reflect the author of the reviewed work, while the
RV field should be the author of the review. The YR field should
be set to the year of the review, not the year of the reviewed
work. While only the AE, YR, RV, and PB fields are required it
is helpful if you can add a TP field which indicates what kind
of book is being reviewed (n=novel, a=anthology, c=collection,
nf=nonfiction). Since review data can be helpful in locating
new data for the ISFDB, the type information is needed to figure
out which file the new entry should be placed in.

<pre>

    -- REVIEWS ----------------
    Voyage {
        AE=|Stephen Baxter|
        YR=|1997|
        RV=|Mark Tiedemann|
        PB=|SFAGEJAN97|
    }
    Infinity's Shore {
        AE=|David Brin|
        YR=|1997|
        RV=|Richard Parks|
        PB=|SFAGEJAN97|
    }
    Acts of Conscience {
        AE=|William Barton|
        YR=|1997|
        RV=|Paul Di Filippo|
        PB=|SFAGEJAN97|
    }
</pre>

<h3><a name="PREPARE3D">Interviews</a></h3>
Interview data can be added to the INTERVIEWS file. The person
being interviewed should be entered into the AE field. The 
interviewer should be entered in the IT field. The YR and PB
fields should be completed as usual. Example:

<pre>

    -- INTERVIEWS -------------
    Ellen Asher: Life at the Science Fiction Book Club {
        AE=|Ellen Asher|
        IT=|Richard Gilliam|
        YR=|1996|
        PB=|MNFCSFT1996|
    }

</pre>

